# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Credentials and secrets  —  Constitution Principle V
#
# Broker and market-data credentials load from the environment or a secret
# store and must never be committed or logged. This block is first because a
# leaked brokerage key is the one mistake in this repo that costs real money.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
secrets.*
credentials.*
broker-config.*
*.credentials.json

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Live account state
#
# Anything naming a real account number or holding live positions stays local,
# even in the paper-only version.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
account.json
account-*.json
positions.json

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Market data
#
# Bulk price history is large and re-downloadable, so it is not source. What
# IS source is the snapshot manifest — the source, date range, and checksum
# that let a backtest be reproduced (FR-020). Keep manifests in
# data/snapshots/ (tracked); put downloaded bulk files in the paths below.
#
# Small pinned CSVs used as test fixtures are deliberately NOT ignored here —
# deterministic backtest tests depend on them being committed.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
data/raw/
data/cache/
data/downloads/
data/vendor/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Run artifacts, journals, and logs
#
# Generated by every backtest and paper session, so they churn constantly and
# would swamp the history. Ignoring them here does not conflict with the
# audit-trail requirement (FR-025) — the append-only record lives on disk, not
# in git. To preserve one specific run as evidence for a performance claim,
# commit it deliberately with:  git add -f runs/<that-run>
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
runs/
logs/
journals/
reports/
*.log

# Local databases (audit log, decision store, cached bars)
*.db
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
*.db-journal
*.db-wal
*.db-shm

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Python
#
# Lockfiles (uv.lock, poetry.lock, requirements.txt) are intentionally absent
# from this list — pinned dependencies are part of what makes a run
# reproducible, so they belong in version control.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.so
.Python
.venv/
venv/
env/
ENV/
build/
dist/
*.egg-info/
.eggs/

# Test and type-checking caches
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.tox/
.nox/
.hypothesis/
.coverage
.coverage.*
coverage.xml
htmlcov/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Notebooks
#
# Strategy research tends to live in notebooks. Checkpoints are noise; the
# notebooks themselves are worth keeping.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.ipynb_checkpoints/
*-checkpoint.ipynb

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Editors and tooling
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# Claude Code machine-local settings (skills and shared config stay tracked)
.claude/settings.local.json

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Operating system
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
Thumbs.db
ehthumbs.db
Desktop.ini
$RECYCLE.BIN/
.DS_Store
